      "id": "503ce7c5-8013-491a-974c-89aa549b6f30",
      "name": "Chat Message",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chatTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [0, 416]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Incoming message:\n{{ $json.chatInput }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are the gatekeeper that decides whether the assistant named Julius should reply to an incoming chat message. Output JSON only: {\"respond\": true|false, \"reason\": \"...\"}.\n\nRULES (in priority order)\n\n1. DIRECT MENTION - ALWAYS RESPOND. If the message explicitly mentions Julius by name, tags Julius, or directly addresses Julius, set respond=true. This has the highest priority. Never reject a message clearly directed at Julius.\n\n2. DIRECT REPLY - RESPOND. If the user is replying to one of Julius's previous messages, respond when their message is directed at Julius or continues the conversation with it.\n\n3. RELEVANT CONVERSATION - USE JUDGMENT. If Julius is not mentioned, decide whether it should participate. Consider whether: the message asks a question Julius can meaningfully answer; it requests help, information, an explanation or an opinion; it clearly continues a conversation involving Julius; Julius can add meaningful value without interrupting the conversation.\n\n4. NORMAL HUMAN CONVERSATION - DO NOT RESPOND. If users are chatting among themselves, joking, greeting each other, discussing personal matters, or having a conversation that does not involve Julius, set respond=false.\n\n5. NO FORCED PARTICIPATION. Do not respond merely because a message contains a question, an interesting topic, or something Julius knows about. A question directed at another person is not automatically an invitation for Julius.\n\n6. AMBIGUOUS MESSAGES. If it is unclear whether Julius should participate, choose respond=false. Never choose silence when rule 1 applies.\n\nCONTEXT: Messages arrive one at a time. Use any recent conversation history provided to judge who is speaking to whom, whether Julius is already part of the conversation, whether the message continues a previous exchange, and whether it is meant for another user. Do not assume every message is intended for Julius."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "2380fd5f-681c-44c1-b2ff-e10b2068ee26",
      "name": "Should Julius Reply",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
